This folder contains scripts that generate a satellite timesereies dataset labelled by hail class.
The timeseries consist of MSG 10.8 micrometer channel. The crops are created over the area where the maximum hail class occurs 
(or if no hail is present centered over the overpass areas). This maximum hail class is assigned as label to the cropped timeseries.
The timeseries are created in such a way that they end with an additional PMW overpass which carries the hail information.

**/config/study_settings.py**
File where the study settings are stored. This needs to be adapted here as they are read in automatically.

**construct_labelled_timeseries.py**
This is the main script to generate the labelled timeseries. When running, everything is generated automatically.
The procedure is as follows:
1. Define your study settings in /config/study_settings.py
2. Run construct_labelled_timeseries.py

**chunk_MWCCH_files.py**
This script contains a function to chunk MWCCH files into groups based on MSG timeseries length. 
It is used in the procedure of the creation of labelled MSG timeseries datasets (see construct_labelled_timeseries.py).

**MWCCH_file_lists_for_studies.py:**
This script creates lists of MWCCH hail probability data files that meet certain criteria. 
For one thing you can extract files for a certain study period (years, months, days).
And for another thing you can set a specific area coverage threshold, so then the list contains 
only files of those overpasses covering at least that percentage of the total EXPATS domain area.
It allows for efficient retrieval of files that meet certain criteria for further analysis.  

**crop_over_hail_or_overpass.py**
Contains methods to crop the MSG timeseries over the maximum hail area.

**plot_chunking_MWCCH_files.py**
Some plots to visualise the number of MWCCH group representing the number of timeseries that can be generated for different study settings.